WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.434
-Welcome back.

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.567
President Joe Biden

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:03.801
is joining us.

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:05.467
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:07.000
President Biden,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.367
what did it feel like
the first time

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:11.000
you walked into the White House
as president?

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.501
What was the first thing
you noticed?

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:17.167
-What I did notice is that

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:21.300
there is a sense
that you realize

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.400
it's not your house,
it's the people's house.

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:26.100
And that sounds corny,
"It's the people's house."

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.234
But you realize
that that's the case.

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:30.300
And one of the things
that I find, Jimmy,

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.400
and I think you really
would associate with this --

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.901
Jill and I feel we come
from middle-class backgrounds.

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:39.133
We both are college graduates
who worked like hell.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:42.267
We had fathers who didn't go --
Anyway.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:44.400
The end result was
that we're not used

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.400
to people waiting on us.
-Yeah.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.701
And so, in the White House,
you know, there's somebody to,

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:52.601
you know, make your breakfast
or someone to pack your clothes

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:54.133
or someone to carry your bag.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:56.734
We now have a deal --
and they're great --

00:00:56.734 --> 00:01:00.300
the guys who run the kitchen
on the second floor is

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.601
we don't have them come in
to do breakfast for us

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:06.334
because there's no need for them
to have to do breakfast for us.

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:10.400
We can make our own eggs
or, you know,

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.801
pour a bowl of
-You make your own eggs?

00:01:12.801 --> 00:01:13.901
-cereal.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.367
Well, I don't.
Jill does.

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:16.467
I couldn't, you know.

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:20.100
I tell you what.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.567
I'll tell you a true story.

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:23.701
-Yeah.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.267
-When Jill was going
to graduate school,

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:27.033
which was her whole life,
it seems,

00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:28.167
[ Laughter ]
when I was a senator,

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:33.033
I'd get home real quickly
and we'd trade off

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:36.267
and my young daughter
would be there

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:39.033
and she'd take off for school,
night school.

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:40.734
Anyway,
to make a long story short,

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.467
my daughter was being
interviewed

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:45.133
when she was about, I don't
know, nine, 10 years old.

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:47.100
Said,
"Can you daddy cook for you?"

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.133
Said, "My daddy can't do much.

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:51.167
He can boil water
and make psghetti,

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:52.300
but he can't do much else."

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:53.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:56.000
-Yeah, exactly right.
-And guess what -- she's right.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.467
She's right.

00:01:57.467 --> 00:02:00.767
-If we talk again, I check in
with you this time next year,

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:02.968
what do you hope we're going
to be talking about?

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:04.901
-I hope we're going to be
talking about how

00:02:04.901 --> 00:02:08.734
we've we've gotten COVID more
under control.

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:10.968
I hope we're going
to be talking about how

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:14.934
we have actually reduced
the burden

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.133
on middle-class folks
financially,

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:19.167
that salaries continue to go up.

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:21.434
I hope we're going to talk about
unemployment still going down.

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:23.467
I hope we're going to be
talking about inflation

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:26.234
being under control.

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:28.467
But, the other thing, Jimmy,

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:32.300
I really hope that we're going
to be able to demonstrate

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:35.634
that we made worldwide progress
on the environment

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:38.901
because I think it's a critical
thing and pray God --

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:41.300
pray God -- we will have passed

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.267
the John Lewis Act
and the Voting Rights Act

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:47.367
because what's going on now
in about 30 states

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.868
is literally un-American.

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:52.200
It's about trying to prevent
people from voting,

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.501
rather than allow them to vote.

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:55.334
So there's a there's
a full plate,

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:56.868
but I think we can do it.

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:59.133
I'm optimistic about the future

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:01.033
and I'm optimistic
about this country.

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:03.334
We are, as I told everybody,

00:03:03.334 --> 00:03:08.234
including everyone from the
leader of China to Russia

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:09.501
and everyone else,

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:11.968
that I don't know anybody
who wouldn't trade places,

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:14.834
a world leader wouldn't trade
places with my job,

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:18.834
versus theirs, because we have
more available to us.

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:20.567
We have more capacity.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:24.100
We have more science
and technology and decency,

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.767
I think, than any country
in the world.

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:29.567
And so I think the sky's
the limit, as to what we can do

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:32.434
in the second quarter
of the 21st century.

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:34.167
[ Applause ]
-Before you go --

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:36.033
[ Cheering and whistling ]

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:38.367
I hope that as well.

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:40.701
I just want to tell you
what an honor it is

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:42.100
to have you on the show tonight.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.367
I'm a very proud American.

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:45.734
Thank you so much
for being here

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:47.701
and, if you ever need me
for anything, don't hesitate.

00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:49.400
I am there for you.
I am there for you.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.434
-Well, Jimmy, Jimmy,

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:53.734
maybe you ought to come down
and have dinner with me.

00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:55.100
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:56.868
[ Cheering and applause ]
I'm coming.

00:03:56.868 --> 00:03:57.934
I'm going right now.
Alright,

00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:59.901
President Biden, everybody.

00:03:59.901 --> 00:04:01.267
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:03.334
Stick around.
I'll be right there.

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:04.000
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.133
♪♪

